    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d410">

                <pb facs="0504" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg422"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 309.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-11-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 14, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received your despatch of the 18th
                    of October, No. 186, in which you give me the substance of a conversation held
                    between yourself and <pb facs="0505" n="423" xml:id="pg423"/> Mr. Drouyn de
                    Lhuys on the 17th ultimo, upon the subject of the re-enforcement of the French
                    army in Mexico by recruiting troops in Egypt.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to say to Mr. Drouyn de Lhuys that the disposition of this
                    matter by the Emperor’s government is received with sincere satisfaction by the
                    government of the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
